.nh
.TH "PB-CONNECT" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-connect - Create and attach to an environment terminal session


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb connect <environment> [new] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Open a durable terminal session on a machine (an "environment") and attach this terminal to
it. Without --session it always creates a fresh session, optionally named with --name; a
session keeps running when you disconnect. Attach to an existing one with --session (its name
or ID), or with pb session attach. --name and --session cannot be combined. A second argument
new is accepted and means the same as leaving --session out; it cannot be combined with
--session.

.PP
The status bar shows connection and recording state: --status-bar auto, on or off,
--status-bar-fullscreen hide or show, --status-bar-theme terminal, dark, light or mono.
--debug shows the pb versions in use. If the connection drops, pb reconnects; at the start of a
line, Enter ~ r reconnects now, Enter ~ . disconnects, and ~~ sends a literal ~.

.PP
This command does not support --json output; it rejects that mode before execution. Use --help --json for structured command help.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	show the pb versions used by this terminal session

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for connect

.PP
\fB--name\fP=""
	name for the fresh terminal session

.PP
\fB--session\fP=""
	attach an existing terminal session by name or ID

.PP
\fB--status-bar\fP=""
	status bar for this attach: auto, on, or off

.PP
\fB--status-bar-fullscreen\fP=""
	status bar in full-screen applications: hide or show

.PP
\fB--status-bar-theme\fP=""
	status bar theme: terminal, dark, light, or mono


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb connect homelab
  pb connect homelab --name deploy
  pb connect homelab --session deploy
  pb connect homelab --status-bar off
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb(1)\fP
